"""What the mixins of the big Qt classes may use of their host.

MainWindow is put together from ~25 mixins (gui/main_*.py, player/main_*.py),
PlaylistTable from three (gui/table_*.py), PlayModePanel and
BigPlayerWidget from one each (player/widgets/*_setup.py). A mixin reaches for attributes and
methods that its host or a sibling mixin defines; on its own the type checker
sees none of them. Each mixin therefore derives from the host class declared
here, for the type checker only (`if TYPE_CHECKING:`; at run time the base is
`object`), and its uses are checked against these declarations.

It cannot be the real class: MainWindow derives from the mixins, so a mixin
deriving from MainWindow would derive from itself. The declarations follow the
real definitions; reportIncompatibleMethodOverride (pyproject.toml) fails when
an implementation no longer matches its declaration here.
"""

